[%# Rendered by this recipe rather than by ufw.  It used to live under ufw and
    name the port and protocol variables, which ufw has never been told: what a
    recipe hands it is rate_limits and nothing else, so both rendered empty and
    the profile came out as

        ports=/

    on every guest -- something ufw lists and no rule anybody can use.  The port
    and the protocol are configured here, so the profile naming them belongs
    here too.

    The section name stays OpenVPN.  /etc/services has openvpn in lower case and
    the check ufw makes is case sensitive, so this one is accepted where a
    lower-case name would be skipped. -%]
[OpenVPN]
title=OpenVPN
description=OpenVPN server, on the port and protocol this domain configured
ports=[% port %]/[% proto %]
